Adreno: the TEV's zero inputs read from the uniform buffer (Qualcomm's shader compiler miscompiles them)

WakerQuest 1.1.3. Qualcomm's Adreno drivers from 0.700 on (Vulkan 512.700; the Quest 3 runs 512.837)
miscompile TEV stages that take a constant zero input: Dolphin's BUG_BROKEN_TEV_COLOR_ZERO (PR #14899,
merged 2026-10-04), where Dolphin on the same headset shows the same wrong dungeon minimap and HUD
buttons as the port. Dolphin replaces colour inputs A and B that are zero with a uniform that is
always 0 (konstLookup[8]); a tester's Snapdragon 8s Gen 3 still showed the bug with that alone.

- webgpu: g_adrenoTevZeroWorkaround, set from the adapter (PCI vendor 0x5143, or a device named
  Adreno), logged once: "adreno TEV zero workaround: on|off (adapter ..., vendor ...)".
- The GX uniform header gets tev_zero (a vec4f after xr_clip, always written as zeros: every GX
  shader's layout, 16 bytes more per draw).
- On Adreno every zero TEV input (colour and alpha, A, B, C and D, and a zero rasterised channel)
  is ubuf.tev_zero instead of the constant, so the driver cannot fold it. C and D too: the miscompile's
  cause is not known, a uniform read costs next to nothing, and the minimap's own alpha (ZERO, A0,
  TEXA, ZERO) and the clipping squares' colour (ZERO, ZERO, ZERO, C0) take zeros in several places.
- build_shader_source's and build_shader's hash take the flag (the source differs on Adreno).

